    body: "# Mediterranean Grain Bowl\n\n**25 min · Plant-forward**\n\n## Why it works\nWhole grains, beans, and colorful vegetables bring fiber and plant protein together, while a lemon-herb dressing adds flavor and healthy fats.\n\n## Ingredients\n- 1 cup cooked quinoa or brown rice\n- 1/2 cup chickpeas, rinsed\n- 1 cup mixed vegetables (cucumber, tomato, bell pepper)\n- 1 handful baby spinach\n- 2 tbsp olive oil\n- 1 tbsp lemon juice\n- 1 clove garlic, minced\n- Pinch of dried oregano, salt, and pepper\n\n## Method\n1. Warm the grains and place them in a bowl as the base.\n2. Add the spinach, chickpeas, and chopped vegetables.\n3. Whisk olive oil, lemon juice, garlic, and oregano into a dressing.\n4. Drizzle the dressing over the bowl and toss gently.\n5. Finish with a pinch of salt and pepper to taste.\n\n## Tip\nSwap the beans, grains, or vegetables for whatever you have on hand — the structure stays the same.\n\n> True Diet provides education, not diagnosis or medical nutrition therapy.",
