    subtitle: "30 min · High protein",
    category: "High protein",
    body: "# Salmon & Colorful Veg Plate\n\n**30 min · High protein**\n\n## Why it works\nSalmon provides protein and omega-3 fats, roasted vegetables add fiber and antioxidants, and a grain or potato rounds out the plate with steady energy.\n\n## Ingredients\n- 1 salmon fillet (about 140 g)\n- 1 cup broccoli and bell pepper, chopped\n- 1/2 cup cooked farro, rice, or roasted potato\n- 1 tbsp olive oil\n- 1/2 lemon\n- Salt, pepper, and dried herbs\n\n## Method\n1. Heat the oven to 200°C (400°F).\n2. Toss the vegetables with olive oil, salt, and pepper; roast for 15 minutes.\n3. Add the salmon to the tray, season, and roast 10–12 minutes more.\n4. Plate the salmon with the vegetables and your chosen grain or potato.\n5. Squeeze lemon over the top before serving.\n\n## Tip\nSalmon can be swapped for any fish or for chicken, tofu, or tempeh.\n\n> True Diet provides education, not diagnosis or medical nutrition therapy.",
