    body: "# Overnight Oats with Fruit\n\n**5 min + overnight · Breakfast**\n\n## Why it works\nOats bring fiber, yogurt adds protein and live cultures, and fruit adds natural sweetness — a practical breakfast that holds up well on busy mornings.\n\n## Ingredients\n- 1/2 cup rolled oats\n- 1/2 cup milk or fortified plant milk\n- 1/3 cup plain yogurt\n- 1 tsp chia seeds (optional)\n- 1/2 cup fresh or frozen berries\n- 1 tsp honey or maple syrup (optional)\n\n## Method\n1. Combine oats, milk, yogurt, and chia seeds in a jar.\n2. Stir well, cover, and refrigerate overnight.\n3. In the morning, top with berries and a little honey if you like.\n4. Stir and enjoy cold, or warm briefly if you prefer.\n\n## Tip\nMake two or three jars at once so breakfast is ready for the next few days.\n\n> True Diet provides education, not diagnosis or medical nutrition therapy.",
