    body: "# Lentil & Vegetable Soup\n\n**40 min · Plant-forward**\n\n## Why it works\nLentils deliver plant protein and fiber, while a base of vegetables and herbs makes a filling, freezer-friendly meal.\n\n## Ingredients\n- 1 cup dried red lentils, rinsed\n- 1 onion, diced\n- 2 carrots, diced\n- 2 celery stalks, diced\n- 2 cloves garlic, minced\n- 1 can (400 g) chopped tomatoes\n- 4 cups low-sodium stock\n- 1 tsp cumin, salt, and pepper\n\n## Method\n1. Soften the onion, carrot, and celery in a little olive oil.\n2. Add the garlic and cumin and cook for one minute.\n3. Add the lentils, tomatoes, and stock; bring to a simmer.\n4. Cook 25–30 minutes until the lentils are tender.\n5. Season to taste and serve, or blend half for a creamier texture.\n\n## Tip\nFreezes well in portions — a good back-up for days you do not want to cook.\n\n> True Diet provides education, not diagnosis or medical nutrition therapy.",
